---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import River from '../components/River.astro';
import ConfluenceMark from '../components/ConfluenceMark.astro';
import RiverLettering from '../components/RiverLettering.astro';
---
<Layout title="Tributary — A river-shaped identity study" description="Original Tributary identity studies exploring natural river shapes, confluences, and converging currents.">
<div class="brand-study wrap">
  <header class="study-intro"><span class="eyebrow">TRIBUTARY / IDENTITY EXPLORATION</span><h1>A river can be<br />the whole language.</h1><p>Its tributaries shape the mark. Its currents connect the diagrams. Black and white give every contribution room to be seen.</p><p class="study-status">Design studies for review. The proposal’s purpose stays the same: royalties returning to creators.</p></header>
  <section class="study-logo" aria-labelledby="confluence-heading"><div class="study-notes"><span class="eyebrow">01 / CONFLUENCE</span><h2 id="confluence-heading">A small mark,<br />with a river inside.</h2><p>Thin tributaries meet at a single gateway. A square marks the contribution, and one stem carries the current forward. The geometry follows the Gateway Flow visual language.</p></div><div class="confluence-specimen"><div class="confluence-lockup"><ConfluenceMark size={92} /><span>tributary.</span></div><div class="mark-sizes"><ConfluenceMark size={24}/><ConfluenceMark size={40}/><ConfluenceMark size={64}/></div></div></section>
  <section class="study-logo" aria-labelledby="meander-heading"><div class="study-notes"><span class="eyebrow">02 / CURRENT</span><h2 id="meander-heading">A name carried<br />by the current.</h2><p>Open letterforms sit within thin converging currents. The same geometry connects a compact mark, wordmark, and larger whitepaper cover.</p></div><div class="meander-specimen"><RiverLettering /><span class="specimen-caption">A wordmark and current study</span></div></section>
  <section class="study-palette" aria-labelledby="palette-heading"><span class="eyebrow">03 / BLACK & WHITE</span><h2 id="palette-heading">Light to read.<br />Dark to flow.</h2><div class="palette-bands"><div class="palette-parchment"><span>White</span></div><div class="palette-vermilion"><span>Paper</span></div><div class="palette-sediment"><span>Silver</span></div><div class="palette-current"><span>Graphite</span></div><div class="palette-canopy"><span>Black</span></div></div><p>White reading surfaces alternate with black flow scenes. Fine white trajectories and square particles carry the identity. Color no longer determines a contribution’s importance.</p></section>
  <section class="study-flow" aria-labelledby="flow-heading"><div class="study-notes"><span class="eyebrow">04 / THE PROPOSED FLOW</span><h2 id="flow-heading">Natural bends.<br />Clear relationships.</h2><p>Fine trajectories bring the confluence into focus. Switch between royalties returning to your project and your code becoming part of other products.</p><p>The paths are illustrative. A measured Sankey chart would need verified amounts and widths proportional to those amounts.</p><a class="text-link" href="/">See it on the creator-focused homepage</a></div><River /></section>
  <section class="study-origin"><span class="eyebrow">REFERENCE TO REASONING</span><h2>The geometry does the work.</h2><p>Your river-lettering reference shows how landscape can supply the shapes of a name. <a href="https://www.metalab.com/work/windsurf">Metalab’s Windsurf identity</a> carries a natural motif across its mark, color, and larger applications. The <a href="https://tympanus.net/codrops/2025/11/17/windsurf-x-metalab-building-a-new-brand-for-the-future-of-ai-coding/">Codrops breakdown</a> helps explain how that motif becomes a wider system. These studies use original shapes for Tributary; they are inspired by river behavior rather than traced from satellite geography.</p><div class="study-film-notes"><article><h3>One shape, many uses.</h3><p>A confluence can connect the small mark, river diagram, and larger landscape artwork.</p></article><article><h3>Contrast gives structure.</h3><p>White surfaces carry reading. Black backgrounds give the fine white currents presence.</p></article><article><h3>Motion explains direction.</h3><p>The royalty switch changes the flow’s arrows. Reduced-motion preferences remove the transition.</p></article></div></section>
</div>
</Layout>
